@page "/Festivals/CrownPavilion"
<HeadContent>
    <PageTitle>Festival of Four Winds: Crown Pavilion! | Convergence Corp!</PageTitle>
    <meta name="description" content="Festival of Four Winds: Crown Pavilion!">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://convergencecorp.net/Festivals/CrownPavilion" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Festival of Four Winds: Crown Pavilion! | Convergence Corp!" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://convergencecorp.net/Festivals/CrownPavilion" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://convergencecorp.net/favicon/android-chrome-512x512.png" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Festival of Four Winds: Crown Pavilion!" />
</HeadContent>
<article class="festival-article">
    
    <h1>CrownPavilion</h1>
    <section>
    <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/CrownPavilion-Banner.png"] style="width:100%;"/>
        <p>
            Originally built in a huge sinkhole known as the Great Collapse, 
            the Crown Pavilion was built to host the Queen's Jubilee, 
            a celebration of Queen Jennah's 10th year of reign over Kryta.
        </p>
        <p>
            The Crown Pavilion opens up during the Festival of the Four Winds,
            which typically starts in Late July or August.
        </p>
    </section>
    <figure style="width:100%; max-width:600px;">
        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/CrownPavilion-Center.png"]  style="width:100%;"/>
        <figcaption>The central island of the Crown Pavilion</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section>
        <h2>Activities!</h2>

        <!-- Boss Blitz -->
        <h3 id="Blitz">Boss Blitz</h3>
        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BossBlitz-Banner800x200.png"] style="width:100%;"/>
        <p>
            The Boss Blitz is the main event of the Crown Pavilion. 
            Each section of the pavilion features a Legendary boss.
        </p>
        <p>
            Killing one of the bosses will pass their special skill to all of the other bosses.
        </p>
        <p>
            Blitz Organizer Grayford prepares the next Boss Blitz, the progress bar can be seen slowly filling in the active events.
            You can donate gold to Grayford to speed up the process,
            5% per 1 gold.
        </p>
        <h3>Bosses</h3>
        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/CrownPavilion-Blitz.png"] style="width:100%;" />
        <div>
            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Baines.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Boom-Boom Baines</figcaption>
                    <blockquote>
                        Working out of EarthLord's Gap, Baines proclivity for explosives and her fiery personality made her an infamous bandit across the human realm.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Bandit_Boon.png"] />
                        Explosive Powder Kegs
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        Explosive Kegs spawn randomly around the boss, explosively exploding after a few a seconds.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Hablion.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Justiciar Hablion</figcaption>
                    <blockquote>
                            One of the founding members of the White Mantle, Justiciar Hablion was a one of Saul D'Alessio's closest friends.
                            After the bloodstone explosion in Bloodstone Fen, his soul now haunts the Colosseum of the Faithful.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Spectral_Displacement.png"] />
                        Spectral Displacement
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        AoEs on the ground randomly teleport players.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Kuraii.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Kuraii the Cruel</figcaption>
                    <blockquote>
                        A ruthless strategist from the Tamini Centaurs of the War King's Greatcamp,
                        Kuraii the Cruel would shoot his enemies with debilitating arrows and retreat into a maze of his own making.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Trample.png"] />
                        Trample
                    </h4>

                    <p>
                        Centuars swarm the arena, trampling anyone in their way.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Pyroxis.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Pyroxis</figcaption>

                    <blockquote>
                        Based on the destroyers that live in the lava floes of Mount Maelstrom,
                        Pyroxis conjures Lava and spits fire.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Firewave.png"] />
                        Firewave
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        Fire scythes shoot out from the boss. They ricochet when hitting a wall.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Sparcus.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Sparcus Firesplash</figcaption>
                    <blockquote>
                        Sparcus Firesplash was a fearsome warrior of the Flame Legion who presided over the Provatum Castrum.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Fiery_Tornado.png"] />
                        Fiery Tornado
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        Fire Tornados roam around, knocking back and burning anyone it crosses paths with.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                
            </div>
            <div class="BossBlitzBossContainer">
                <figure class="BossFigure">
                    <img class="BlitzBossPic" src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzBosses/Wiggin.png"] />
                    <figcaption>Wiggin the Wicked</figcaption>
                    <blockquote>
                        Wiggin the Wicked was a versatile fighter of the Convington Pirates that have taken over Laughing Gull Island.
                        His signature move was to throw a bomb at his opponents while dodging them.
                    </blockquote>
                </figure>
                <div class="BossSpecial">
                    <h4>
                        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/BlitzSkills/Bombs_Away.png"] />
                        Bombs Away
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        Cannon shots drop from the sky in an X pattern.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                
            </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Pavilion Pursuit (race) -->
        <h3 id="Pursuit">Pavilion Pursuit</h3>
        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/PavilionPursuit-Banner.png"] style="width:100%;" />
        <p>
            Race through each sector of the Crown Pavilion on your trusty mount as you avoid environmental traps and enemies!
        </p>
        <p>
            The Pavilion Pursuit is a race that starts 2 minutes after the Boss Blitz finishes. 
            You can signup for the race immediately after the last boss of the blitz is defeated.
        </p>
        <p>
            There is also a time trial version that you can do at anytime.
        </p>
        <h4>Related Achievements:</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/E8959D0B4C417C7207AC27D2D20A0FA67A11D95F/2015705.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Pavilion Pursuer - Finish the race or time trial within 2 minutes.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/9BED5B1BC4DC043E72CA9A6F07704D4EF875655E/2015706.png" style="width:48px;" />
                (Annual) Practiced Pursuit - Complete 5 laps in the race event or the time trial. 
                The race event grants extra progress.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/9BED5B1BC4DC043E72CA9A6F07704D4EF875655E/2015706.png" style="width:48px;" />
                (Repeatable) Ace Racer - Finish 3 festival races in the Labyrinthine Cliffs or Crown Pavilion.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- Queen's Gauntlet -->
        <h3 id="Guantlet">Queen's Gauntlet</h3>
        <img src=@Assets["/images/Festivals/FourWinds/Pavilion/Gauntlet-Banner.png"] style="width:100%;" />
        <p>
            The Queen's Guantlet is a series of fights that you must challenge solo.
            To advance a tier of the gauntlet, you must defeat all of the champions within your current tier.
        </p>
        <h4><img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/4A0D55430A717CE5BA7F98BEC20B92053646520A/619594.png" style="width:48px;" />Queen's Gauntlet Entrance Tickets</h4>
        <p>
            Challenging a boss costs an Entrance Ticket.
            Adding gambits also costs an additional ticket per gambit added.
        </p>
        <p>
            Tickets are purchasable from the Gauntlet Ticket Vendor for 35 Festival Tokens and 20 silver per 5 tickets.
            Doing the Boss Blitz also gives tickets.
            Tickets also have a chance to drop from all the mobs in the pavilion.
        </p>
        <h4>Queen's Gauntlet Achievements (no specific tier):</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;"/>
                First Blood - Defeat 1 Queen's Guantlet opponent.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Blood Sport Enthusiast - Complete 1 Combat Challenge.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Blood Sport Connoisseur - Complete 7 Combat Challenges.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Gauntlet Contender - Defeat 12 Queen's Gauntlet bosses.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Gauntlet Favorite - Defeat 12 Queen's Gauntlet bosses with at least one gambit active.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/9BED5B1BC4DC043E72CA9A6F07704D4EF875655E/2015706.png" style="width:48px;" />
                (Annual) Gauntlet Contender - Defeat 12 Queen's Gauntlet bosses.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Tier 1</h3>
        <h4>Halmi Hammerfell</h4>
        <p>
            Avoid his big smash by interupting it or moving behind him.
        </p>
        <h4>Doobroosh</h4>
        <p>
            The more you hit Doobroosh, the bigger and stronger he gets. 
            Kite him around the arena as he doesn't have any ranged attacks.
        </p>
        <h4>Windcaller Kieldia</h4>
        <p>
            Every few seconds Kieldia summons another tornado that stays in the arena permanently.
            She doesn't do much damage herself but will eventually perma knockback you to death with the help of her tornados.
        </p>
        <h4>Suriel the Blazing Light</h4>
            <p>
                Suriels' Blazing Light makes her invulnerable.
                Suriel loses Blazing Light by walking through the shadow circles on the ground.
                She reapplys Blazing Light by using Solar Flare.
                Solar Flare is an undodgable, unblockable, arena wide AOE that will oneshot and knock you down.
                Avoid the damage portion of Solar Flare by standing in the shadow circles to gain the Shrouded by Darkness effect.
            </p>
        <h4>Tier 1 Achievements:</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Doobroosh Tranquilizer - Defeat Doobroosh after he gains max stacks of Hormonal Imbalance
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Candle in the Wind - Defeat Windcaller Kieldia with On Fire gambit active.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Light Snuffer - Complete the first tier of the Queen's Guantlet.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Tier 2</h3>
        <h4>Tyre Ragemaw</h4>
        <p>
            Tyre Ragemaw deals damage Inversely to how much HP he has. 
            This means low damage at 100%, 10x damage below 10%.
        </p>
        <h4>Masticus</h4>
        <p>
            Masticus has extremely high HP. Run around collecting the orbs to increase your own damage.
        </p>
        <h4>Salazan</h4>
        <p>
            Salazan puts a fire ring on the ground around you. 
            Leaving the ring of fire will kill you instantly. 
            Avoid his flame attacks while staying within the ring.
            This fight is much easier with a ranged build.
        </p>
        <h4>The crew of the pirate ship Ravenous</h4>
        <p>
            The crew of the pirate ship Ravenous consists of 4 members. When one of them are killed, they pass on a skill to the rest of them.
        </p>
        <p>
            Captain Barnicus - Inspires his crewmates
            Grants Swashbucklers's Daring, Periodically dodge attacks.
        </p>
        <p>
            First Mate Gaets - High Damage
            Grants Envenomed Blades - Attacks apply poison.
        </p>
        <p>
            Stitches - Heals Allies
            Grants Good Nutrition - Gain Health every second.
        </p>
        <p>
            Master Gunner Adil - Calls Cannon Strikes
            Grants Ace in the Hole - Everyone gets pistols.
        </p>
        <h4>Tier 2 Achievements:</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Savage Brute - Defeat Masticus with max stacks of Bloodlust active.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Pirate Punisher - Complete the second tier of the Queen's Gauntlet.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Tier 3</h3>
        <h4>Subject 7</h4>
        <p>
            An ooze that splits into more oozes when it loses HP. 
            Defeat subject 7 quickly or you could get overwhelmed by the number of oozes.
        </p>
        <h4>Deadeye Dunwell</h4>
        <p>
            Deadeye Dunwell places mines all over the arena. 
            Running into one will deal massive damage.
            Either bring a ranged build or navigate the mines to get to Dunwell.
        </p>
        <h4>Strugar and Chomper</h4>
        <p>
            A ranger and pet pair, Strugar and Chomper fight together. Strugar throws meat that Chomper can eat to get stronger. 
            You can also eat this meat to deny it to Chomper, but eating too many will stun you for a few seconds.
        </p>
        <h4>Liadri the Concealing Dark</h4>




        <h4>Tier 3 Achievements:</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Risk Taker - Win 1 third tier match with an active gambit.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Triple Threat - Win 1 third tier match with three active gambits.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                High Stackes Gambler - Win 1 third tier match with five active gambits.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Humble Victor - Win a third tier challenge with active Frailty and Squeamish gambits.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Blobs, Schmobs - Defeat Subject 7 without killing any oozes.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Meatless Murderer - Defeat Strugar and Chomper while denying Chomper any delicious meat.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Darkness Illuminator - Complete the third tier of the Queen's Gauntlet.
            </li>
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Light Up the Darkness - Defeat Liadri the Concealing Dark after striking her with eight orbs of blazing light.
            </li>
            
        </ul>

        <h3>Special Tier</h3>
        <h4>Master of Lightning</h4>
        <h4>Pallia the Errant</h4>
        <h4>Champion Gladiator Waine</h4>
        <h4>Suriel the Radiant Light</h4>
        <h4>King Turai Ossa</h4>
        <h4>Special Tier Achievements:</h4>
        <ul style="margin-top:0px;">
            <li>
                <img src="https://render.guildwars2.com/file/DC4FE57C1BD6DD0D3A4763FC1F31DAB94DFF4A09/619304.png" style="width:48px;" />
                Kingslayer - Defeat King Turai Ossa.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

</article>
